> This is a popular misconception about Nethack. Coverting before the 
> quest is doable and will not affect the outcome of the game.

	Wrong. Converting before the Quest will prevent you from gaining
entry to it, which means you can't get the Bell of Opening, can't
perform the Invocation, can't get the Amulet, and can't ascend.

	You may be thinking of putting on a helm of opposite alignment
before the Quest, which will not prevent you from winning the game,
because you can get back to your original alignment just by taking the
helm off (after uncursing it), with no permanent effects other than
possible loss of (replacable) divine protection. Converting yourself on
an altar, however, is permanent, irreversible, and one-time-only, and
will render the game unwinnable if done before you have the Bell in
hand.

